  "facts": [
    "Hida Tunnel, stretching 10.7 kilometers through Mominukasan mountain, ranks as Japan's third-longest road tunnel after Yamate and Kanetsu, and sits proudly at twelfth place worldwide.",
    "Completed in 2008, Hida Tunnel opened its concrete arteries to traffic, dramatically shortening travel between Hida city and Shirakawa village and cutting through the rugged Mominukasan mountain.",
    "Carrying the Tōkai‑Hokuriku Expressway (E41), Hida Tunnel carves a 10.7‑km spine through Mominukasan mountain, a feat that showcases Japan's engineering prowess in navigating the Gifu prefecture's rugged terrain."
  ],
